# Chaos: living water and lava (O206; src/client/item.h/.cpp, luafunctions_client.cpp and Lua:
# mods/client_settings/classes/dataset.lua, options/graphics.otui; after 0001-0127). Owner overlay module game_visualfx
# (client/MANIFEST.md "Visual effects", "Living water and lava (O206)") does the rest. Water and lava ground sprites get a
# subtle animated shimmer through two fragment shaders (data/shaders/chaos_liquid_*.frag), so the map looks more modern; the
# sprite's own colours and alpha are kept, so every biome keeps its water and lava.
#  * Item keeps a table client id -> kind (1 water, 2 lava; Item.clearLiquidIds, Item.addLiquidId, sent once by the module
#    from visualfx_logic.lua L.LIQUID) and the switch (Item.setLiquidShimmer).
#  * Item::draw (the map one): an item with no shader of its own whose client id is in the table draws through the existing
#    ThingType::drawWithShader / DrawQueueItemThingWithShader path (the one items with setShader use) with chaos_liquid_water
#    or chaos_liquid_lava. The cost is one byte lookup per drawn item and, for a liquid tile, one shader draw instead of a
#    batched textured rect. Option off, table empty or shader missing -> the plain draw, as before. No extra pass, no Lua per tile.
#  * The ripple is under one texture pixel and fades to nothing at the tile edge (v_Norm, as chaos_map_vertex.frag), so a
#    sprite never reads the next frame of its sheet; the wave phases are whole multiples of pi across the tile, so they run on
#    over the seam between two tiles.
#  * Option liquidShimmer (default on), Options > Graphics under the five visual effects of 0126/0127 (the panel grows
#    from 105 to 124 px).
# Checked: applies cleanly after 0001-0127 to the base client tree (no fuzz) and item.cpp and luafunctions_client.cpp pass a
# syntax-only compile; not run in a client.
